  "whatArrived": "The idea that invisible living organisms, not bad air or chance, caused infectious disease, first suggested by Ignaz Semmelweis's 1847 handwashing results,[1] then given a mechanism by Louis Pasteur's research, then turned into surgical practice by Joseph Lister's antiseptic method.[2]",
