  "firstResistance": "Semmelweis's own colleagues rejected his findings for over a decade, in part because accepting them meant accepting that doctors' own hands had been killing patients. He died in 1865, still largely unrecognized, and it took Pasteur's later research to give his observation a mechanism doctors would accept.[1][2]",
