  "whatArrived": "The electric telegraph, opened commercially between Washington and Baltimore in May 1844, able to carry a short text message in minutes rather than the days or weeks a letter or rider needed.",
  "whatItEntered": "Markets, newspapers, and governments that had built their routines around the travel time of a physical message, and whose sense of current information was set by how fast a person or document could move.",
